        "t1": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p><strong>From the River District to the islands</strong></p><p>Fort Myers sits on the south bank of the Caloosahatchee, with the River District downtown. McGregor Boulevard's royal palms run past the Edison and Ford winter estates toward the Gulf. Across the river, Cape Coral is a grid of canals, and many lots there have a seawall, a pool and a screened lanai. Sanibel lies over the causeway, Fort Myers Beach on Estero Island, and Pine Island behind Matlacha. Bonita Springs, Estero and Naples continue the pattern to the south.</p><p>Hurricane Ian came ashore in Lee County in September 2022. Since then, many waterfront homes have been repaired or rebuilt higher, which puts balconies and stairs well above grade and under the guard rules. Salt air reaches every one of them, so hardware choice matters. Inland, Gateway, Lehigh Acres and San Carlos Park add pool homes without the salt but with the same summer humidity.</p>"
          }
        },
        "t2": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p><strong>Lee County rules for decks, balconies and pools</strong></p><p>Lee County is not in the High-Velocity Hurricane Zone. It is a coastal county with high design wind speeds under the Florida Building Code, 8th edition (2023). Fort Myers, Cape Coral, Sanibel, Bonita Springs and Fort Myers Beach each have a building department; unincorporated addresses go to Lee County Community Development. Each reviews railing attachments, so have the engineering documents ready.</p><p>The residential code sets a 36-inch guard for a house deck, balcony or stair landing more than 30 inches above grade. Condos on the beach and in the River District need 42 inches. Pool barriers follow the Residential Swimming Pool Safety Act: at least 48 inches on the outside, with gates that close on their own and open away from the pool. The 46-inch panel gives that 48 inches. Our <a href=\"/pages/florida-building-code-for-glass-railings\">Florida building code page</a> has the references; confirm with your building department before ordering.</p>"
          }
        },
        "t3": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p><strong>Delivery to Fort Myers and DIY installation</strong></p><p>Standard panels are processed in 2 to 3 business days and arrive in 5 to 10 business days by freight carrier with a liftgate. The trucks reach Cape Coral, Sanibel, Pine Island and Fort Myers Beach by road. The crate comes down to your driveway wherever you are in Lee County. Custom sizes take 2 to 3 weeks in transit after processing. Orders over 3,000 dollars ship free, and the price at checkout is final, with no duties, tariffs or hidden fees from the border crossing.</p><p>The system is designed for DIY. Spigots fix to a concrete pool deck or to the wood framing of a raised house, with screws sold separately. The <a href=\"/pages/glass-railing-installation-guide\">installation guide</a> and videos cover the whole job; a standard railing takes about 4 hours. Report any damage within 3 days of delivery and before installation, and we replace or refund it at no cost.</p>"
          }
        }
